    <briefdescription>
<para>Configuration controlling GPU acceleration for clustering algorithms. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>When <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_gpu_clustering_config_1a4c54a32258ea8a9a768204032220e701" kindref="member">use_gpu</ref></computeroutput> is true and CUDA is available, clustering will use GPU kernels for the distance computation phase:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>k-Means: ECEF 3D projection + FAISS GPU FLAT_L2 for the assignment step.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>DBSCAN: GPU Haversine batch kernel for precomputing the adjacency matrix; BFS expansion runs on CPU using the precomputed matrix. Only datasets with <computeroutput>n ≤ <ref refid="struct_gpu_clustering_config_1a08b4f09e160419310bf9a285b80a2569" kindref="member">gpu_dbscan_max_n</ref></computeroutput> are eligible (larger datasets fall back to CPU to stay within VRAM limits).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>When <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_gpu_clustering_config_1a4c54a32258ea8a9a768204032220e701" kindref="member">use_gpu</ref></computeroutput> is false, or when no CUDA device is present, the CPU path is used transparently — callers do not need to check this at the call site. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
